## Output agreement with {{ reference }}

| Engine |{{ " Concurrency |" if levels | length > 1 }} Top-1 match | Beam overlap (worst request) | Rank match | Max score Δ |
| --- |{{ " ---: |" if levels | length > 1 }} ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
{% for row in agreement %}
| {{ row.name }} |{{ " %s |" | format(row.k) if levels | length > 1 }} {{ row.top1 | pct }} | {{ row.overlap | pct }} ({{ row.overlap_min | pct }}) | {{ row.rank | pct }} | {{ "%.4g" | format(row.score_delta) }} |
{% endfor %}

Over the measured requests of each engine's first round{{ ", at each concurrency" if levels | length > 1 }}. Top-1 match: identical best beam. Beam overlap: the share of the reference's beams that the engine also returned, in any order, as the mean over requests and, in parentheses, the lowest request. Rank match: the share of ranks with identical tokens. Max score Δ: the largest difference in cumulative log-probability among shared beams; with a catalog, engines normalize over different token sets, so it can be nonzero when the beams agree.

